# Independent review: submit followed by remotely recorded status wait

Verdict: no blocking finding in the reviewed execution bridge. The diff was reviewed against base fe03602; exact final source snapshots are under source/.

Reviewed execute/_execute, seven submission tests, README and the reused submit/wait_remote contracts against chapter 15's transaction budget, 600-second status cap, uncertainty and journal ordering requirements. The bridge validates the supplied remaining transaction budget, measures submission elapsed time, stops before polling when that budget is exhausted, and passes the returned receipt head plus at most min(600, remaining) seconds into remote waiting. Submission exceptions propagate without starting a status wait. No retry, new transaction or public-success inference is added.

Independent execution: all seven tests passed normally and with Python -O. The real temporary Git-server integration checks that the remote receipt exists before the synthetic status GET, uses one synthetic POST and one status response, and returns the same remote observation/head. Deterministic budget tests cover 60 seconds minus 17, exact exhaustion at 60, and the 600-second cap from a 3600-second transaction; uncertain creation does not poll. Existing submission failure/ordering regressions also run in this suite.

Additional independent probe verifies both ordinary submission validation/CAS-style failure and CreationUnknown produce zero wait calls, six invalid budgets start neither submission nor polling, and fractional remaining budgets preserve the newly returned receipt head. commands.json, probe-results.json and raw output preserve evidence. These injected collaborators and clocks do not constitute live API timing tests.

The existing transport/Git startup and cleanup limitations still apply; this is not a hard realtime guarantee. Authorization, provenance, durable intent eligibility, remote protection, lock ownership and resume/reconciliation remain publisher responsibilities. The report records API observations, not current public identity, smoke success, recovery eligibility or LKG promotion. No real Pages API or NEPL3 remote write occurred, and the reviewer made no implementation edits.
